#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM gratis tentang informasi dan komputasi kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Superdense coding"
msgstr "Superdense coding"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore mapsto */}\n"
"Superdense coding is a protocol that, in some sense, achieves a complementary aim to teleportation.\n"
"Rather than allowing for the transmission of one qubit using two classical bits of communication (at the cost of one e-bit of entanglement), it allows for the transmission of two classical bits using one qubit of quantum communication (again, at the cost of one e-bit of entanglement).\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore mapsto */}\n"
"Superdense coding adalah protokol yang, dalam beberapa hal, mencapai tujuan yang saling melengkapi dengan teleportasi.\n"
"Alih-alih memungkinkan transmisi satu qubit menggunakan dua bit klasik komunikasi (dengan biaya satu e-bit entanglement), ini memungkinkan transmisi dua bit klasik menggunakan satu qubit komunikasi kuantum (sekali lagi, dengan biaya satu e-bit entanglement).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In greater detail, we have a sender (Alice) and a receiver (Bob) that share one e-bit of entanglement.\n"
"According to the conventions in place for the lesson, this means that Alice holds a qubit $\\mathsf{A}$, Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B}$, and together the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is in the state $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$.\n"
"Alice wishes to transmit two classical bits to Bob, which we'll denote by $c$ and $d$, and she will accomplish this by sending him one qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lebih rinci lagi, kita punya pengirim (Alice) dan penerima (Bob) yang berbagi satu e-bit entanglement.\n"
"Sesuai konvensi yang berlaku untuk pelajaran ini, ini berarti Alice memegang qubit $\\mathsf{A}$, Bob memegang qubit $\\mathsf{B}$, dan bersama-sama pasangan $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ berada dalam keadaan $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$.\n"
"Alice ingin mengirimkan dua bit klasik kepada Bob, yang akan kita sebut $c$ dan $d$, dan dia akan melakukannya dengan mengirimkan satu qubit kepadanya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is reasonable to view this feat as being less interesting than the one that teleportation accomplishes.\n"
"Sending qubits is likely to be so much more difficult than sending classical bits for the foreseeable future that trading one qubit of quantum communication for two bits of classical communication, at the cost of an e-bit no less, hardly seems worth it.\n"
"However, this does not imply that superdense coding is not interesting, for it most certainly is.\n"
msgstr ""
"Wajar untuk menganggap hal ini kurang menarik daripada yang dicapai oleh teleportasi.\n"
"Mengirim qubit kemungkinan akan jauh lebih sulit daripada mengirim bit klasik untuk masa mendatang yang dapat diperkirakan, sehingga menukar satu qubit komunikasi kuantum dengan dua bit komunikasi klasik, dengan biaya e-bit pula, hampir tidak tampak sepadan.\n"
"Namun, ini tidak berarti bahwa superdense coding tidak menarik, karena memang sangat menarik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fitting the theme of the lesson, one reason why superdense coding is interesting is that it demonstrates a concrete and (in the context of information theory) rather striking use of entanglement.\n"
"A famous theorem in quantum information theory, known as *Holevo's theorem*, implies that without the use of a shared entangled state, it is impossible to communicate more than one bit of classical information by sending a single qubit.\n"
"(Holevo's theorem is more general than this.\n"
"Its precise statement is technical and requires explanation, but this is one consequence of it.)\n"
"So, through superdense coding, shared entanglement effectively allows for the *doubling* of the classical information-carrying capacity of sending qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sesuai tema pelajaran ini, salah satu alasan mengapa superdense coding menarik adalah bahwa ia mendemonstrasikan penggunaan entanglement yang konkret dan (dalam konteks teori informasi) cukup mencolok.\n"
"Sebuah teorema terkenal dalam teori informasi kuantum, yang dikenal sebagai *teorema Holevo*, mengimplikasikan bahwa tanpa penggunaan keadaan yang terjalin bersama, tidak mungkin untuk mengkomunikasikan lebih dari satu bit informasi klasik dengan mengirimkan satu qubit.\n"
"(Teorema Holevo lebih umum dari ini.\n"
"Pernyataan tepatnya bersifat teknis dan memerlukan penjelasan, tapi ini adalah salah satu konsekuensinya.)\n"
"Jadi, melalui superdense coding, entanglement bersama secara efektif memungkinkan *penggandaan* kapasitas membawa informasi klasik dari pengiriman qubit.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Protocol {#protocol}"
msgstr "Protokol {#protocol}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following quantum circuit diagram describes the superdense coding protocol:\n"
msgstr "Diagram Circuit kuantum berikut menggambarkan protokol superdense coding:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Superdense coding circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/superdense-coding.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Superdense coding circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/superdense-coding.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In words, here is what Alice does:\n"
msgstr "Dalam kata-kata, inilah yang Alice lakukan:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $d=1$, Alice performs a $Z$ gate on her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ (and if $d=0$ she does not).\n"
msgstr "Jika $d=1$, Alice melakukan Gate $Z$ pada qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ miliknya (dan jika $d=0$ dia tidak melakukannya).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $c=1$, Alice performs an $X$ gate on her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ (and if $c=0$ she does not).\n"
msgstr "Jika $c=1$, Alice melakukan Gate $X$ pada qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ miliknya (dan jika $c=0$ dia tidak melakukannya).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alice then sends her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ to Bob.\n"
msgstr "Alice kemudian mengirimkan qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ miliknya kepada Bob.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What Bob does when he receives the qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ is to first perform a controlled-NOT gate, with $\\mathsf{A}$ being the control and $\\mathsf{B}$ being the target, and then he applies a Hadamard gate to $\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
"He then measures $\\mathsf{B}$ to obtain $c$ and $\\mathsf{A}$ to obtain $d$, with standard basis measurements in both cases.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yang Bob lakukan ketika menerima qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ adalah pertama melakukan Gate controlled-NOT, dengan $\\mathsf{A}$ sebagai kontrol dan $\\mathsf{B}$ sebagai target, lalu dia menerapkan Gate Hadamard ke $\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
"Dia kemudian mengukur $\\mathsf{B}$ untuk mendapatkan $c$ dan $\\mathsf{A}$ untuk mendapatkan $d$, dengan pengukuran basis standar pada kedua kasus.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis {#analysis}"
msgstr "Analisis {#analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The idea behind this protocol is pretty simple:\n"
"Alice effectively chooses which Bell state she would like to be sharing with Bob,\n"
"she sends Bob her qubit, and Bob measures to determine which Bell state Alice chose.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ide di balik protokol ini cukup sederhana:\n"
"Alice secara efektif memilih keadaan Bell mana yang ingin dia bagikan dengan Bob,\n"
"dia mengirimkan qubit miliknya kepada Bob, dan Bob mengukur untuk menentukan keadaan Bell mana yang Alice pilih.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, they initially share $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$, and depending upon the bits $c$ and $d$, Alice either leaves this state alone or shifts it to one of the other Bell states by applying $\\mathbb{I}$, $X$, $Z$, or $XZ$ to her qubit\n"
"$\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Artinya, mereka awalnya berbagi $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ dan bergantung pada bit $c$ dan $d,$ Alice meninggalkan keadaan ini apa adanya atau menggesernya ke salah satu keadaan Bell lainnya dengan menerapkan $\\mathbb{I},$ $X,$ $Z,$ atau $XZ$ ke qubit miliknya\n"
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes XZ) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^-\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes XZ) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^-\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bob's actions have the following effects on the four Bell states:\n"
msgstr "Tindakan Bob memiliki efek berikut pada empat keadaan Bell:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 01\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto -\\vert 11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 01\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto -\\vert 11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This can be checked directly, by computing the results of Bob's operations on these states one at a time.\n"
msgstr "Ini bisa diperiksa secara langsung, dengan menghitung hasil operasi Bob pada keadaan-keadaan ini satu per satu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, when Bob performs his measurements, he is able to determine which Bell state Alice chose.\n"
"To verify that the protocol works correctly is a matter of checking each case:\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, ketika Bob melakukan pengukurannya, dia bisa menentukan keadaan Bell mana yang Alice pilih.\n"
"Untuk memverifikasi bahwa protokol bekerja dengan benar adalah masalah memeriksa setiap kasus:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $cd = 00$, then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$. He transforms this state into $\\vert 00\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 00$.\n"
msgstr "Jika $cd = 00$, maka keadaan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ ketika Bob menerima $\\mathsf{A}$ adalah $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$. Dia mengubah keadaan ini menjadi $\\vert 00\\rangle$ dan mendapatkan $cd = 00$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $cd = 01$, then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle$. He transforms this state into $\\vert 01\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 01$.\n"
msgstr "Jika $cd = 01$, maka keadaan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ ketika Bob menerima $\\mathsf{A}$ adalah $\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle$. Dia mengubah keadaan ini menjadi $\\vert 01\\rangle$ dan mendapatkan $cd = 01$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $cd = 10$, then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle$. He transforms this state into $\\vert 10\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 10$.\n"
msgstr "Jika $cd = 10$, maka keadaan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ ketika Bob menerima $\\mathsf{A}$ adalah $\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle$. Dia mengubah keadaan ini menjadi $\\vert 10\\rangle$ dan mendapatkan $cd = 10$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $cd = 11$, then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle$. He transforms this state into $-\\vert 11\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 11$. (The negative-one phase factor has no effect here.)\n"
msgstr "Jika $cd = 11$, maka keadaan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ ketika Bob menerima $\\mathsf{A}$ adalah $\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle$. Dia mengubah keadaan ini menjadi $-\\vert 11\\rangle$ dan mendapatkan $cd = 11$. (Faktor fase negatif satu tidak berpengaruh di sini.)\n"
